# Beehive App Completion & Enhancement Plan

## 1. Project Overview
Beehive is a marketplace and product recommendation app that allows users to:
- Store and manage product images and details
- Categorize products and link them to e-commerce or other websites
- Browse a marketplace of user-shared products (anonymized)
- Receive product recommendations
- Support multiple currencies and countries

## 2. Current State
- UI/UX partially designed
- User images not yet stored in filesystem
- Marketplace and recommendation features not fully implemented
- Currency and localization support not complete

## 3. System Design & Implementation Plan

### A. User Image Storage
- Store user-uploaded images in the device filesystem (using `path_provider` and `image_picker`)
- Reference image paths in the database (Firebase/SQLite)

### B. Product Categorization & Linking
- Allow users to add products to categories
- Enable direct linking to external websites (e-commerce, etc.)
- Auto-create categories if not present

### C. Marketplace Feature
- Display anonymized product listings from all users
- Show product details and purchase links
- No user-identifiable information displayed

### D. Recommendation System (AI Capabilities)
- Suggest products based on user interests, browsing, and purchase history
- Use collaborative filtering or content-based filtering (can use TensorFlow Lite or integrate with a cloud AI service)
- Optionally, recommend trending products in the marketplace

### E. Multi-Currency & Localization
- Detect user country and currency (using device locale or user selection)
- Convert prices using a currency API (e.g., exchangerate-api.com)
- Localize UI strings for supported languages

### F. Additional AI Features (Future Scope)
- Visual search: Let users search for products by uploading a photo
- Chatbot for product recommendations and support
- Sentiment analysis on product reviews
- Personalized notifications and offers

## 4. Detailed TODO List
1. Complete UI/UX for all screens
2. Implement image storage in filesystem
3. Build product add/edit with category and link support
4. Implement marketplace (anonymized product feed)
5. Add product recommendation engine
6. Integrate multi-currency and localization
7. Test on multiple devices and countries
8. Prepare Play Store assets (screenshots, description, privacy policy)
9. Finalize and publish

## 5. Documentation & Explanation
- System design diagrams (component, data flow)
- Explanation of AI recommendation logic
- Security and privacy considerations
- How to extend the app with more AI features

---

**This document serves as a roadmap for completing and enhancing the Beehive app for Play Store release.**
